!Sample_submission_date = Apr 03 2019
!Sample_last_update_date = May 01 2019
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = plasmid DNA
!Sample_organism_ch1 = synthetic construct
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 32630
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = sample type: plasmid pool
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = HAP1 cells were transduced with the GECKOv2 lentiviral library, and at 24-hours post infection, puromycin (2.5 ug/ml final concentration) was added to the media to select for transduced cells.
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = HAP1 and HAP1-derived cell lines and pools were maintained in Iscove's Modified Dulbecco's Medium (IMDM) supplemented with 10% FBS and 100 units/mL penicillin, 100 µg/mL streptomycin (Invitrogen).
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = genomic DNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Genomic DNA was prepared using the Gentra Puregene kit (Qiagen #158767)
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Integrated sgRNAs were amplified by PCR for 24 cycles. For sgRNA sequencing, 2 ug of gDNA per PCR reaction was used as template, and four reactions were pooled per sample to ensure sufficient representation of integrated sgRNAs. The resulting amplicon was diluted and further amplified in a second-round PCR to add Illumina adaptor sequences and sample-specific index barcodes.
!Sample_description = plasmid DNA
!Sample_data_processing = counts
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: counts
